s($,"biS","a6m",()=>A.b([A.fr("Prepare a clean demo","Resets the simulation, clears history and builds 30 minutes of simulated readings at the Saadiyat Island tower site.","Prepare",new A.aKL(),!1),A.fr("Introduce the site",'"This is a simulated construction site on Saadiyat Island, Abu Dhabi, with one virtual heat-stress station. It is a November morning, the cool season. Everything is labelled as simulated, and every number comes from the backend."',"Show overview",new A.aKM(),!1),A.fr("Show live conditions",'"The station measures air, wet-bulb and globe temperature. HeatGuard combines them into WBGT, the standard heat-stress index, using the outdoor formula because the site is in direct sun."',"Open live monitoring",new A.aKN(),!1),A.fr("Select a crew doing heavy work",'"Concrete Crew A is doing heavy work. Because they are acclimatized, NIOSH\'s exposure limit applies. Today they are within it."',"Open Concrete Crew A",new A.aKV(),!0),A.fr("Change acclimatization",'"Suppose half the crew are new to the site. For unacclimatized workers NIOSH sets a lower alert limit, so the same heat is now a concern, and the explanation says exactly why."','Set "not acclimatized"',new A.aKW(),!0),A.fr("Increase the heat",'"Now the day heats up: +4 \xb0C and stronger sun. Watch the level rise. HeatGuard tells us which work/rest schedule is needed to stay within the limit."',"Raise heat",new A.aKX(),!0),A.fr("A protective alert is raised",'"An alert is generated automatically, with the explanation and recommended actions. Repeats are suppressed, and alerts are never cleared automatically."',"Open alerts",new A.aKY(),!1),A.fr("Acknowledge the alert",'"The supervisor acknowledges it. If nobody does, it escalates."',"Acknowledge Crew A alert",new A.aKZ(),!1),A.fr("Record an intervention",'"We record the protective action: a 15 min work / 45 min rest rotation and lighter tasks. The crew is reassessed immediately, and the level drops."',"Record rotation",new A.aL_(),!1),A.fr("Wearable strain, with consent",'"Four workers in Crew A chose to share wearable data. Badge CA-02 now shows a sustained high heart rate (NIOSH: above 180 minus age). The supervisor sees only the badge to check on, never the values."',"Simulate strain on CA-02",new A.aL0(),!1),A.fr("A worker reports symptoms",'"A worker taps \u201cI feel unwell\u201d in their own language. A first-aid escalation is raised at once. Confusion or collapse would trigger the 998 emergency path."',"Report dizziness (Rebar B)",new A.aL1(),!1),A.fr("OHS view: who sees what",'"Switching to the occupational health role shows the symptoms and signal values. Supervisors never see them. The OHS officer records the outcome; there is no \u201ccleared to work\u201d button."',"Switch to OHS role",new A.aKO(),!1),A.fr("Shamal dust storm",'"Back to the supervisor. A shamal coats the globe and dries the wick. HeatGuard spots the fouled sensor, asks for maintenance and shows \u201cunavailable\u201d rather than a misleading reading."',"Start dust event",new A.aKP(),!1),A.fr("Clean the station",'"After cleaning, readings are trusted again and assessments resume. Low battery is handled the same way: a warning first, then \u201cunavailable\u201d, never green."',"Clean station",new A.aKQ(),!1),A.fr("Plan the shift",'"A July morning at 07:00. The shift plan looks ahead for each crew: do the heaviest work before it gets too hot, start a work/rest schedule on time, stop strenuous work when no schedule is enough, and respect the midday break. Crew level only, no individual data."',"Open the shift plan",new A.aKR(),!1),A.fr("UAE midday break",'"Summer in Abu Dhabi: we jump to 12:35 on a July day. Besides the heat-stress level, HeatGuard checks the UAE midday break: outdoor work in direct sun is not permitted from 12:30 to 15:00, 15 June to 15 September. It raises a separate compliance alert."',"Jump to 12:35 in July",new A.aKS(),!1),A.fr("Show the evaluation",'"Finally, 13 repeatable synthetic scenarios, including dust, battery failure and worker strain, are checked against ground truth: early warning, no missed alerts, and zero minutes showing safe while data were missing. Software verification, not clinical validation."',"Run evaluation",new A.aKT(),!1),A.fr("Worker app",'"Workers carry their own app, separate from this dashboard: on the phone browser or as an Android or iOS app. They see their crew\'s heat level in English, Arabic, Urdu or Hindi, choose whether to share wearable signals, report feeling unwell and call 998. No tracking."',"Open worker app",new A.aKU(),!1)],A.aw("C<P0>")))
